# The measurement overlay of a profile (planning/esp32-platform-profiles.md, "measure"): keys
# that only observe, given after the profile's own fragments, for an image that is run to be
# measured. Declared in profiles.json, where the keys it may touch are listed; the guard holds
# the build to them, so an image built with it is the profile's and not a scratch build.
#
#   SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="$(sink_profile.py defaults p4-rev1 --overlay measure)"
#
# The AC-4 decoder hashes the bit pattern of every sample it hands over (ac4.pcm_hash, the
# probe's FNV-1a), which is what says whether the float output equals the host's
# (testdata/ac4-probe-pcm-hashes.json). The profile locks it off: hashing costs time, which the
# decoder measures and takes back out of its own, so the speed figure is not moved by it. A play's
# location can still ask for no hash (?hash=off), so one image measures both.
#
# The board suite's AC-4 rows need it: a row whose line carries no pcm_hash says so and is not
# held to a pin. Nothing else is set here, and a key added to this file is a key to declare.
CONFIG_ICLFORGE_EXAMPLE_AC4_PCM_HASH=1
